<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://eric-laurence.github.io/notes/posts/theorem-demo/index_files/figure-html/cell-2-output-1.png" width="507" height="282" class="figure-img"></p>
<figcaption><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Csin%20x"> vs.&nbsp;its degree-5 Taylor polynomial at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?0">.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The approximation is excellent near <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?0"> and visibly drifts as <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%7Cx%7C"> approaches <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cpi"> — which is the whole point of a <em>local</em> Taylor expansion.</p>


